  "highlights": [
    {
      "title": "Overview",
      "value": "<p>The Fachhochschule des Mittelstands (FHM) is a private, state-recognized university of applied sciences in Germany, specifically designed to meet the needs of medium-sized enterprises (the German \"Mittelstand\"). Established in 2000, it has grown into one of the most successful private universities in the country. You will find that FHM focuses heavily on practical, career-oriented education, ensuring that what you learn in the classroom is directly applicable to the professional world. The university is organized into several key departments, including Psychology, Education &amp; Social Sciences, Business, Communication, Technology, and Sport &amp; Health.</p>",
      "image": null,
      "highlightType": "General"
    },
    {
      "title": "Student life",
      "value": "<p>At FHM, you will experience a \"family atmosphere\" characterized by small learning groups and close personal contact with professors. The university emphasizes a colorful and lively campus life where you can engage in interactive learning both online and on-campus. Because FHM is deeply integrated with the SME sector, you will often find yourself collaborating with industry partners on real-world projects. Support is always at hand through the International Student Advisory Service, which helps you navigate the German education system and cultural adaptation.</p>",
      "image": null,
      "highlightType": "General"
    },
    {
      "title": "Accommodation",
      "value": "<p>While FHM does not typically own large-scale on-campus dormitories like some traditional universities, they provide extensive support to help you find a home. You can choose from various options such as:</p><ul><li>Private Student Residences: Many students opt for modern apartments in cities like Berlin or Cologne.</li><li>Flat Shares (WG): A popular and budget-friendly choice in Germany where you share a kitchen and bathroom with other students.</li><li>Private Rentals: The university advisory service provides detailed information and tips for navigating local housing markets.</li></ul><p>For more stays options, you can check out Edvoy <a href=\"https://edvoy.com/student/stays\">Stays</a></p>",
      "image": null,
      "highlightType": "General"
    },
    {
      "title": "Facilities",
      "value": "<ul><li>Library The FHM library system is highly digitalized to support flexible learning. You will have access to over 28,000 physical resources and a massive digital collection including over 36,000 e-books and millions of specialist articles via databases like Springer, Statista, and WISO.</li><li>Sports While the university doesn't have a centralized sports department, it organizes varied activities at individual locations. You can join running groups, football tournaments, and even cross-location ski trips.</li><li>Laboratories You will have access to specialized facilities depending on your campus. For instance, the Institute for Hydrogen Technology in Düren and the Institute for Cyber Security and Digital Innovation provide world-class environments for research and technical training.</li><li>Cafeteria Most FHM campuses are centrally located, meaning you have access to various on-campus dining areas and nearby local cafes and restaurants that cater to the student community.</li></ul>",
      "image": null,
      "highlightType": "General"
    }
  ],
